 "response": "Tido's budget is now **$3,930K**.\n\n**Method**\n1. Only Finance Office entries change the budget. All other messages were ignored, including the many \"Heard\u2026\" and \"Pretty sure\u2026\" notes.\n2. For each withdrawal, I traced its chain to the end, since a withdrawal can itself be withdrawn. Examples:\n   - #0575 withdraws #0175, which withdraws #0031, which withdraws #0011. So #0011 is cancelled and #0007 (+$303K) still applies.\n   - #0955 withdraws #0727, which withdraws #0361, which withdraws #0295. That leaves #0093 standing, so #0028 (+$423K) is cancelled.\n   - #1528 withdraws #0792, which withdraws #0100. That leaves #0100 standing, so #0083 (\u2212$596K) is cancelled.\n   - #0633 withdraws #0576, which withdraws #0554. That leaves #0554 standing, so #0036 is cancelled and #0010 (+$3K) still applies.\n3. Starting from the $1,650K set in #0001, I applied every remaining increase and decrease in record order.\n\n**Checkpoints in the running total**\n| After record | Budget |\n|---|---|\n| #0045 | $2,462K |\n| #0190 | $4,805K |\n| #0539 | $2,535K |\n| #0650 | $1,423K |\n| #0820 | $3,942K |\n| #1115 | $4,050K |\n| #1599 (final) | $3,930K |\n\nThis is a long hand calculation over about 1,600 records. The method is sound, but a small arithmetic slip in one step is possible.\n\nANSWER: $3930K",
